{
 "icone": "🌒",
 "titulo": "The World",
 "blocos": [
  {
   "t": "prose",
   "texto": "The Shadow World is not another planet. It is **our world**, pressed against the real one, separated by a thin film — almost invisible, almost impassable. On one side are the *impure*: ordinary people, who see nothing. On the other, the Shadows and the Illuminated."
  },
  {
   "t": "prose",
   "texto": "Caught in between are the few **Marked** children — touched as infants by a nameless force that leaves a spiral scar on the body. The mark draws everything in: the Shadows that feed on pain, and the gold-lit Illuminated who have hated them since the cradle."
  },
  {
   "t": "card",
   "variant": "purple",
   "titulo": "The Shield",
   "corpo": [
    {
     "t": "prose",
     "texto": "Every Marked child is born inside an invisible film that blocks the Shadows' direct touch. It shouldn't exist — it is an error, something *broken*."
    },
    {
     "t": "prose",
     "texto": "The Shield cracks a little with every **Special Night** and every death tied to the Marked one. What happens when it breaks completely has not yet been documented."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "card",
   "variant": "blue",
   "titulo": "The Special Nights",
   "corpo": [
    {
     "t": "prose",
     "texto": "Rare events where Shadows and Illuminated manifest at once. They always come with mass deaths and local collapses of reality."
    },
    {
     "t": "prose",
     "texto": "The Marked draw these nights — and the gaps between them shorten before great tragedies. Minus has survived three."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "card",
   "titulo": "The other side",
   "corpo": [
    {
     "t": "prose",
     "texto": "The *Shadow World* is a distorted reflection of the real one, where the Shadows exist in solid form. Every city has its own version, each with a different level of corruption."
    },
    {
     "t": "prose",
     "texto": "Entering that plane drains a human's body and mind within minutes. Minus crosses anyway — time runs differently there, and it lets him cover impossible distances in seconds."
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
